-- title:
--   Directed isomorphism characterized by nongeneration
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be an abelian group. Suppose $a,d,h\in G$, $2h=0$, $h\ne0$, and the image of $d$ in $G/\langle h\rangle$ has exact order three. Assume $\langle a,d,h\rangle=G$ and set $S=\{a,a+d,a+d+h\}$, $T=\{a,a-d,a-d+h\}$. Then
--
--   $$\operatorname{Cay}(G,S)\cong\operatorname{Cay}(G,T)\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\langle a,h\rangle\ne G.$$
--
--   An isomorphism here is any bijection of vertices preserving directed arcs $x\to x+s$. This applies without a finiteness assumption.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, https://github.com/alexcour/couret-finite-verifications/blob/65b828d9ffd016ce2a1b05403f303fa5f948c10f/research/correspondants_20261013/lean/CayleyTwoColourAbelian.lean#L1060-L1075, lines 1060–1075; source file SHA-256 c9643d6e3a677d5a903623825d50a309d87175a21ace2b7ab56939d9189f13b1; theorem Couret.CayleyDoublet.abelianThreeIso_iff_nongeneration_of_quotient_order_three

